Source: sniplab
Section: utils
Priority: optional
Maintainer: snip release bot <41898282+github-actions[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>
Build-Depends:
 debhelper-compat (= 13),
 cargo (>= 1.89),
 rustc (>= 1.89),
 gcc,
 git
Standards-Version: 4.6.2
Rules-Requires-Root: no
Homepage: https://github.com/gitkeniwo/snip

Package: sniplab
Architecture: any
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}
Description: filesystem-native snippet library and agent-friendly CLI
 snip keeps snippets as ordinary files that can be searched, diffed, edited,
 and versioned with Git. It provides a JSON-speaking command-line interface
 and a three-pane terminal browser. The installed command is named snip.
